  "corrections": {
    "deliveryLatency": "E1 s2 published 30 / 46 / 46 / 30 seconds for jobs 1033 / 1034 / 1035 / 1037, from polling getJob every 15 s. Those numbers are close to CREATED -> SUBMITTED, not FUNDED -> SUBMITTED: the poll loop started when the job was created, and create plus budget plus fund is three transactions of the buyer's own before the provider can see anything. The honest figure for the agent's work is funded -> submitted, and it is SHORTER, so the correction is against our own interest on the agent side and is made anyway.",
    "gas": "protocol s2 predicted a six-transaction hire at ~0.00012 tBNB from an observed gasPrice of 0.1 gwei. Every transaction in this window settled at effectiveGasPrice 0, so the true buyer-side gas cost of every hire is exactly 0 tBNB. Gas USED is real and is reported; gas PAID was zero. A testnet with a zero gas price is not evidence about mainnet economics and the report must not present it as such.",
    "jobStatus": "E1 s2 marked job 1033 COMPLETED. Its own artefact says SUBMITTED, and the chain says the job was submitted and later settled by the buyer. The E1 cell was wrong and is corrected there."
  },
