  "limitations": [
    "Block timestamps have one-second resolution and a BSC block is produced roughly every 0.75 s on chain 97, so each latency below carries about +/-1 s. That is an order of magnitude better than the +/-15 s poll it replaces.",
    "funded -> submitted is the interval in which the provider could act. It is not the provider's compute time: a watcher polls the commerce contract, so part of the interval is that poll's own period, which we cannot see.",
    "The buyer's own minutes — writing the task sentence, requesting the quote, deciding to fund — are outside every figure here and were never stopwatched.",
    "effectiveGasPrice was 0 on every transaction. No mainnet cost claim can be derived from this."
  ],
